-- title:
--   Supersingular valuation ring over small constants with smooth-point packages (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and $\kappa$ the residue field of the valuation subring $A$.
--
--   **Data and arithmetic hypotheses.** Fix a prime $q$ together with the hypothesis $hq2 : q = 2$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; and a prime $\ell_0$ with $\ell_0 \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_0 \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $(q : \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ is a non-unit of $A$, and put $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. The field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\kappa$ generated over $\kappa$ by the Laurent series `jqModC κ` of $j$ and by its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion substitute `jqNModC κ M'`. A finite set $W$ of places of this field over $\kappa$ is given, and `hW` states that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. of those places $w$ which are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in the set `ssJSet q κ`. An element $s \in W$ is fixed.
--
--   The intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change (coefficientwise embedding, then adjunction) of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}_d(j_q)$ for $d \mid M'$; the field `fieldBar q M'` is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, that is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the former together with a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the latter whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of functions with nonzero residue, such that an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $A$ if and only if its image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, residues of constants are the images of their $A$-residues, and every nonzero $f$ admits a constant scaling landing in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies $R_0$ with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The field of small constants.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$ ($h\pi$). Writing $A \cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the hypotheses require: `hdvr`, that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, that it is a henselian local ring; `hres`, that its residue field is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and tame element.** $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Layers.** $\iota$ is a type, $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with each $K_n$ finite-dimensional over $k_0$, and $A_n$ is a valuation subring of $K_n$ with $x \in A_n \iff x \in A$ for all $x \in K_n$ (`hAn`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** The field `fieldBar q M'` is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Then there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following eight properties.
--
--   (1) $F_0$ together with the constants generates everything: the join of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $F_0$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   (2) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (4) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) There is an element $t \in W_0$ which is residually transcendental in the following sense: for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then every coefficient of $p$ has image in $W_0$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (6) $W_0$ is centred at the place $s$: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j_q)$, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion `hle` lies in $F_0$, lies there in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose $A$-residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that image and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (7) Level-equivariance: for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — the automorphism characterised by `IsLevelAutBar`, matching the action of $\gamma$ on $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ under embeddings sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, and the identity if no such automorphism exists — maps $F_0$ into itself, and for $f \in F_0$ with image again in $F_0$ one has $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (8) For every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ that is a $\kappa$-algebra and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with a surjective residue map onto $\mathrm{FSS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, membership of constants governed by $A$, residues of constants given by their $A$-residues, and every nonzero element scalable by a constant into $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue) such that for all $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers} \iff f \in W_0$, the following two assertions hold.
--
--   (8a) *Drinfeld identification of the reduced field.* For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, assuming that the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[x_0,x_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`: there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{FSS}$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ of the subgroup generated by the operators `hFunctionFieldAction q κ ⟨(1, ζ)⟩` for $\zeta \in C_s$, such that $\mathrm{card}\,C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` — namely `jWidthChar q` of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$, which for $q = 2$ is $12$ if that value is $0$ and $1$ otherwise, divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s` — and such that $e$ intertwines the level action with the Drinfeld action: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, given that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,u) \mapsto \det g \cdot u^{q+1}$ with values in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$), one has, for all $x \in \mathrm{FSS}$, that $e$ applied to $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` at $x$ equals, inside the Drinfeld function field, the image of $e(x)$ under `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$.
--
--   (8b) *Ends and smooth-point packages at every layer.* There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, and for each place $Q$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$ and each layer $n \in \iota$ a subring $S_n(Q)$ of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring map $\varphi_n(Q) : A_n[X] \to S_n(Q)$, a ring map $\chi_n(Q) : S_n(Q) \to \kappa$ and a set $D_n(Q)$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that $|N| = q+1$ and such that for every $Q \notin N$ the following hold.
--
--   First, for every layer $n$: (i) the reduction map $A_n \to \kappa$ is surjective; (ii) the image of every $a \in A_n$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $S_n(Q)$; (iii) $\varphi_n(Q)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; (iv) $\varphi_n(Q)(C\,a)$ is that image, for every $a \in A_n$; (v) $\chi_n(Q)(\varphi_n(Q)(C\,a))$ is the $\kappa$-residue of $a$; (vi) $\chi_n(Q)(\varphi_n(Q)(X)) = 0$; (vii) for every $c \in A_n$ with zero residue there is exactly one ring map $\chi : S_n(Q) \to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi_n(Q)(C\,a)) = a$ for all $a \in A_n$, with the $\kappa$-residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_n(Q)(f)$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_n(Q)(X)) = c$; (viii) every $f \in S_n(Q)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_n(Q)(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; (ix) $\varphi_n(Q)(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of its $R$-residue equals $1$; (x) a place $P$ belongs to $D_n(Q)$ precisely when $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_n(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for every $f \in S_n(Q)$ the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if $\chi_n(Q)(f) = 0$; (xi) for every ring map $\chi : S_n(Q) \to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_n(Q) \circ C$ and reducing to $\chi_n(Q)$, there is exactly one place $P \in D_n(Q)$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = \chi(f)$ for all $f \in S_n(Q)$; (xii) for every $P \in D_n(Q)$ and every $f$ in the join of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_n$ with $F_0$, one has $f \in P.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_n(Q)$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \ne 0$; (xiii) every nonzero $f$ in that join with $P.\mathrm{ord}(f) = 0$ for all $P \in D_n(Q)$ satisfies $c f = u$ for some nonzero $c \in K_n$ (via its image) and some unit $u$ of $S_n(Q)$; (xiv) every $f$ in that join which lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P \in D_n(Q)$ lies in $S_n(Q)$; (xv) there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q)$ such that every $f \in S_n(Q)$ satisfies $f h = g$ with $g$ and $h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the images of all elements of $A_n$, and with $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n(Q)$.
--
--   Secondly, the layers are compatible: the subrings are monotone, in that $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies $S_n(Q) \le S_{n'}(Q)$, and moreover (i) for $K_n \le K_{n'}$, $S_{n'}(Q)$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_n(Q)$ together with the images of all elements of $A_{n'}$; (ii) for all $n, n'$ the elements $\varphi_n(Q)(X)$ and $\varphi_{n'}(Q)(X)$ coincide in `fieldBar q M'`; (iii) for $K_n \le K_{n'}$ and $f \in S_n(Q)$, $\chi_{n'}(Q)$ of the image of $f$ equals $\chi_n(Q)(f)$.
--
--   Finally, three global clauses: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, any layer $n$ and any place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'`, membership of $P$ in both $D_n(Q)$ and $D_n(Q')$ forces $Q = Q'$; for $Q \notin N$, every layer $n$ and every $P \in D_n(Q)$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of $j_q$; and, for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $\tau$ preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every place $Q$: the place $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q$ lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does, and if $Q \notin N$ then for every layer $n$ the translate `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)`, that is $\{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D_n(Q)\}$, equals $D_n(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q)$.
--
--   This is the small-constant-field ($k_0$-level) form of the construction of the supersingular component of the stable model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ in residue characteristic $q = 2$, with $M'$ rigidified by an auxiliary prime $\ell_0 \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$: it produces a discrete valuation ring on a $k_0$-rational subfield centred at a chosen supersingular place $s$, the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) description of its reduced function field with stabiliser of order the width of $s$, and, away from $q+1$ ends, étale smooth-point data and residue discs at every finite layer of the tower. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_of_eq_two_of_dvd), which converts these packages into semistable charts for the regular prolongation.
